text:
Wealth is a comfort to every person;
yet each must distribute it generously
if they wish to obtain honor before the Lord.

Ice is very cold and immeasurably slippery;
it gleams, glass-clear, most like gems,
a floor made by frost, fair to behold.

The oak on earth is food for the flesh of humankind;
it travels often over the gannet’s bath. The ocean tests
whether the oak possesses noble fidelity.

Yr is joy and honor for every prince and noble;
it is fair on a horse, steadfast on a journey,
a piece of war-gear.
